{
  "id": "frequency-time-words",
  "level": "a1",
  "area": "Every day",
  "title": "How often? always, usually, sometimes, never",
  "tagline": "Never 0%, always 100%: the words that say how often something happens.",
  "cefr": "A1",
  "exam": [
    "Speaking Part 1 — questions about your free time",
    "Reading Part 5 — open cloze (grammar gaps)"
  ],
  "why": "How often something happens is one of the first things people ask about your life: <i>How often do you play sport?</i> Words like <i>always, usually, sometimes, never</i> and phrases like <i>on Mondays</i> or <i>at the weekend</i> let you answer with real detail, not just yes or no.",
  "hook": {
    "text": "It's Sunday morning. Nadia texts Sofia: \"What do you do at the weekend?\" \"I <b>always</b> play football on Saturdays,\" says Sofia. \"I <b>never</b> do sport on Sundays — I <b>usually</b> read. <b>How often</b> do you swim?\" \"<b>Twice a week</b>,\" says Nadia, \"on Tuesdays and Fridays.\"",
    "ask": "Find four different frequency words in the story. Which one means 0% of the time?"
  },
