  "can_do": [
    "I can use always, usually, sometimes and never in the right place in a sentence.",
    "I can ask and answer <i>How often…?</i> with phrases like <i>twice a week</i> or <i>every day</i>.",
    "I can use <i>at, on</i> and <i>in</i> with times, days and months."
  ],
  "summary": [
    "Frequency words go before the main verb: <i>I always play football</i>.",
    "With be, frequency words go after it: <i>She is never late</i>.",
    "<b>How often…?</b> asks about frequency; answer with <i>once/twice a week, every day, on Mondays</i>.",
    "Use <b>at</b> for times and night, <b>on</b> for days and dates, <b>in</b> for months and longer periods.",
    "The most common order, from 0% to 100%: <i>never, sometimes, usually, always</i>."
  ]
